235	\section{Threshold DGP Simulation}
236	\label{sec:threshold_dgp}
237	
238	To test whether threshold-type misspecification explains the non-significant oracle $\gamma$, we simulate data under step-function contamination DGPs where items are affected only above exposure thresholds of 0.3, 0.5, and 0.7 (three cutoffs, ten seeds each). Under these DGPs, the linear 2PL+$\gamma$ specification overestimates rather than attenuates the contamination effect (ratio 1.09 to 1.33 relative to the true $\gamma$), while PPP remains in the acceptable range (0.50 to 0.56). This rules out threshold-type misspecification as an explanation for the non-significant oracle $\gamma$ under a unidirectional effect assumption. Bidirectional item-level effects (positive for some items, negative for others) could still produce a near-zero pooled $\gamma$, but this collapses to the heterogeneity interpretation (\S\ref{sec:domain_differential}). The simulation uses uniform exposure distributions; real RRF exposure is right-skewed (mean$=$0.041), so the quantitative overestimation magnitude may differ, but the qualitative direction (overestimation, not attenuation) is robust.
239	
240	\section{ARC IRT Results}
241	\label{sec:arc_irt}
242	
243	ARC-Challenge IRT results are reported separately due to marginal model fit (PPP$=$0.003 at $J=16$). The smaller item pool (1,172 vs.\ 14,042 for MMLU) and more homogeneous difficulty distribution contribute to structural misfit: the 2PL+$\gamma$ model cannot adequately capture the item response patterns. Under this caveat, the ARC baseline comparison ($J=16$, 300 RRF items) yields: B0-Raw MAE$=$0.007, B3-Vanilla2PL MAE$=$0.015, B4-LinearRegression MAE$=$0.012 ($\tau = 0.731$, best rank correlation), B6-DCR MAE$=$0.314 (systematic overcorrection), ContamCal MAE$=$0.020. The pattern mirrors MMLU: raw accuracy dominates on MAE because the aggregate contamination effect (${\sim}$0.7pp) is smaller than correction noise. Domain-level $\gamma$ estimation on ARC is unreliable at all tested configurations ($J=8$, 13, 16; PPP $< 0.05$ in all cases).
244	
245	\section{Full Baseline Comparison}
246	\label{sec:full_baselines}
247	
248	Table~\ref{tab:baselines} (main text) reports B0, B3, and ContamCal under the Qwen2.5 pooled configuration ($J=16$ for MMLU/ARC, $J=24$ for GSM8K which retains 0.5B). Table~\ref{tab:full_baselines_arc} presents the complete seven-baseline comparison on ARC under a pooled 0.5B+1.5B configuration ($J=8$, S1-only exposure). This configuration differs from the main analysis ($J=16$, RRF exposure): the smaller ensemble and single-signal exposure limit comparability with MMLU results; these results are included for completeness. Table~\ref{tab:full_baselines_gsm8k} presents GSM8K baselines at 0.5B scale.
