\end{table}

In contrast to the pooled analysis where $\hat{\gamma}$ shifts 2.6$\times$ across priors, Social Sciences $\hat{\gamma}$ varies only 1.2$\times$ ($-$0.43 to $-$0.51), with $P(\gamma<0) \geq 97.95\%$ in all cases.

